From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 17:54:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 069/148] fix(witness): key the worktree guards on shape, not
 the 'polecats' tree name (gcp-elv3)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Both witness cleanup guards gated on a hardcoded `polecats` path literal, so
the entire `views/` worktree tree was invisible to both. The reaper required a
`*/polecats/*/worktrees/*` glob; the home audit required the home's parent
directory to be literally `polecats`. gascity does not keep every agent home
under `polecats/` — a rig running view lanes gets a second tree at
`<rig>/views/<view-home>`, whose homes and per-bead children are byte-identical
in shape and differ only in the tree name. Both gates dropped those paths before
the bulk read and before any `record`, so winnow's 4 view homes and 16 view
worktrees emitted nothing at all: `/views/` appears in 0 of 1293 reap-log
entries across every rig and all time, while `/polecats/` accounts for all 1293.
Today that is accumulation only — the witness hand-checked all 16 — but the
guards are the only thing that would tell us when it stops being benign, and a
view worktree holding genuinely unpublished work emits no
`worktree_unpublished_kept` either. The failure mode is undetectable, not
absent; same class as gcp-ac59, gcp-ivgn and gcp-fyjk.

Both gates now test the SHAPE, per the reporting witness's constraint. The
reaper takes `<agent-home>/worktrees/<bead-id>` where the home is itself
`<lane-tree>/<agent>` two levels under the rig's worktree root; the home audit
takes that same home shape. One definition, shared, so the next lane tree
gascity names is covered on the day it appears — a second `views` literal would
only move the blind spot. The depth is a pack invariant rather than an
observation: `agents/polecat/agent.toml` declares work_dir
`.gc/worktrees/{{.Rig}}/polecats/{{.AgentBase}}` and `agents/refinery/agent.toml`
declares `.gc/worktrees/{{.Rig}}/refinery`, which is what keeps the refinery's
own `refinery/worktrees/<bead-id>` directories out of the reaper's candidate set
now that the tree name no longer does it.

Two exclusions the removed literal was carrying by accident are now named
outright, because keyed on shape alone they are load-bearing:

- The MAIN worktree. A rig rooted at any path ending `<...>/worktrees/<name>`
  matches the per-bead shape exactly and, if clean and published, would clear
  every remaining gate. git lists the main worktree first; it is skipped.
- The refinery's per-bead worktrees, via the home-shape depth above.

KNOWN WIDENING, stated rather than hidden: every rig also has a `crew/` tree,
and crew workspaces are namepool slots of exactly the home shape, so the home
audit now enumerates them. That is a real behaviour change on rigs running no
view lanes, and it is the price of having no tree literal — excluding crew again
needs a name, which is the bug this closes. A respawned crew slot inherits an
abandoned checkout exactly the way a polecat slot does, so the coverage is not
obviously wrong; every gate still applies unchanged (live session, uncommitted
work, unpublished commits, any child worktree all defer), and both sweeps remain
dry-run-only, so the widened `home_removal_pending` set is something to read
across a few cycles before anyone wires `--no-dry-run`. Filed as follow-up work
for the witness to accept or reject deliberately.

Validation: both suites cycled red -> green on new cases. Reaper —
`test_lane_trees_other_than_polecats_are_enumerated` (a `views/` home plus an
invented `nextlane/` tree, both reaped, both recorded, with the in_progress and
agent-home cases still kept) and `test_a_non_agent_worktree_named_like_a_bead_is_not_reaped`
(rig root planted at a path with the exact per-bead shape and a closed-bead
leaf; deleting the MAIN_WT line fails it). Home audit —
`test_lane_trees_other_than_polecats_are_audited` (same two trees, with the
refinery worktree and rig root still untouched and absent from the log). The
pack-asset inventory now pins the structural segments and refuses a `case` arm
globbing any tree name. Full gastown shell suite, tests/ pytest (122 passed, 7
skipped), shellcheck -x on every changed script, go vet, golangci-lint,
validate_registry.py and go test all green.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
